title: "OSDR ChatBot: An Evidence-Grounded Discovery, Schema-Guardrail, and Release Radar Hub for NASA Open Science Data Repository Multi-Omics Research"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Gaston
    family-names: Dana
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-1011-860X"
    affiliation: "Independent Software Architect; Collaborator, NASA OSDR AIML Analysis Working Group"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gastondana627/OSDR_Chatbot"
url: "https://osdr-chatbot-kappa.vercel.app/"
abstract: >-
  OSDR_Chatbot is an open-source, evidence-grounded web application and
  TypeScript/Python service suite for NASA Open Science Data Repository (OSDR)
  study discovery, Analysis Working Group (AWG) multi-omics comparison,
  cross-mission p >> n schema contract generation, Brain AWG 3D scikit-bio
  ordination exploration, LEO dosimetry SAA/GCR pass auditing, and automated
  8-hour OSDR Release Radar monitoring.
keywords:
  - NASA OSDR
  - space biology
  - multi-omics
  - SANS
  - scikit-bio
  - LEO dosimetry
  - scientific software
  - TypeScript
  - React
